  "data": {
    "body": "A mass of $2 \\, \\text{kg}$ is attached to the end of a spring that is stretched $2 \\, \\text{m}$ by a force of $100 \\, \\text{N}$. At time $t = 0 \\, \\text{s}$, the mass is set in motion from its equilibrium position with initial velocity $v_0 = 20 \\, \\text{m/s}$.\n\n(a) Let $x(t)$ be the displacement (in meters) of the mass at time $t$ (in seconds). Write down an initial value problem for $x(t)$.\n(b) Solve the initial value problem from part (a). What are the amplitude and frequency of $x(t)$?",
    "solution": "(a) $x'' + 25x = 0, \\quad x(0)=0, \\; x'(0)=20$\n(b) Amplitude = $4$, Frequency = $\\frac{5}{2\\pi}$",
